      <h2>
        What We Actually Work On
      </h2>

      <p>
        Whatcom County has an unusual mix of heating systems for a region its
        size. There are century-old homes in central Bellingham with ductwork
        installed decades after the houses were built. There are newer homes in
        Ferndale where original furnaces are now reaching the age when control
        boards and blower motors begin to fail.
      </p>

      <p>
        Beyond the cities, many rural properties around Everson, Lynden and
        Custer still rely on propane, oil or electric heating because natural
        gas is unavailable. At the same time, more homeowners are choosing heat
        pumps as an efficient alternative.
      </p>

      <p>
        We work on all of it. Older furnaces, heat pumps, oil systems, propane
        equipment, and heating systems installed in tight crawl spaces are part
        of our everyday work. Rather than recommending replacement because the
        equipment is old, we prefer to diagnose the problem properly and repair
        it whenever it makes financial sense.
      </p>

